"An end user of a tenant: someone who signs in through that tenant's issuer (not a console admin)."
type TenantUser {
  id: ID!
  email: EmailAddress!
  name: String
  emailVerified: Boolean!
  "False once a console admin disabled the user: no sign-in."
  active: Boolean!
  createdAt: DateTime!
  "Whether the user holds a TOTP second factor (tenant viewer). Never the secret or the codes."
  secondFactor: UserSecondFactor!
  "The standard profile fields (OpenID Connect Core 5.1); a field not set is null."
  profile: UserProfile!
}
"""
Everything the console holds about one user, for a data-access (GDPR) request:
their profile, the values of their attributes (hidden ones included, flagged),
their roles, their grants and their sessions. Never a secret or a code.
"""
type UserDataExport {
  exportedAt: DateTime!
  profile: TenantUser!
  attributes: [ExportedAttributeValue!]!
  roles: [ExportedRole!]!
  grants: [UserGrant!]!
  sessions: [UserSession!]!
}

"A role a user holds, by name, with its assignment date."
type ExportedRole {
  role: String!
  assignedAt: DateTime!
}

"A user's TOTP second factor, as an admin may know it."
type UserSecondFactor {
  "True once the factor is active: the user's sign-in by code, link or social asks for it."
  enabled: Boolean!
  "The recovery codes not yet used; null without an active factor."
  recoveryCodesLeft: Int
}

"""
A page of a tenant's users, oldest first; `nextCursor` is `null` on the last.
With `email` the page holds that one user, or none.
"""
type TenantUserPage {
  items: [TenantUser!]!
  nextCursor: String
  "How many users match the filter in all (the whole pool without one), not the page's size."
  totalCount: Int!
}

"""
One standing session of a user (not revoked, not lapsed). Never carries the
token. The console admin cannot tell which one is the viewer's own: it
reads another tenant's users, so there is no `current` flag.
"""
type UserSession {
  id: ID!
  "The browser or device the sign-in came from (its User-Agent, cut at 256 characters); `null` on a session opened before it was recorded."
  device: String
  createdAt: DateTime!
  "When the session last proved who it is (the sign-in, or a step-up)."
  authenticatedAt: DateTime!
  "When the session last renewed (at most once a day); `null` on an older session."
  lastUsedAt: DateTime
  expiresAt: DateTime!
}

"A pending invitation into a tenant's user pool. The code only goes by e-mail."
type UserInvitation {
  id: ID!
  email: EmailAddress!
  invitedAt: DateTime!
  expiresAt: DateTime!
}

"What a user allowed an application to do (an OAuth grant), standing only."
type UserGrant {
  id: ID!
  clientId: String!
  "The client's name, or `null` when the client was deleted since."
  clientName: String
  "The resource (audience) the grant is for."
  resource: String!
  scopes: [String!]!
  createdAt: DateTime!
  "When the scopes were last set by a consent."
  updatedAt: DateTime!
}

"""
A user as the role member picker shows them: who, nothing more. No status, no
flags, no dates.
"""
type UserLookupResult {
  id: ID!
  email: EmailAddress!
  name: String
}

"""
What a tenant admin may change on a user: the name and the standard profile
fields. The e-mail address is not editable; its verified flag is
`setUserEmailVerified`, the phone's `setUserPhoneVerified`. A field left out is
kept; null (or a blank text) clears a profile field.
"""
input UpdateUserInput {
  "The display name: 1 to 200 characters once trimmed. Left out or null keeps it."
  name: String
  "1 to 100 characters once trimmed."
  givenName: String
  "1 to 100 characters once trimmed."
  familyName: String
  "1 to 100 characters once trimmed."
  nickname: String
  "E.164 (`+14165550123`). A number that differs from the stored one starts unverified."
  phone: String
  "A BCP 47 language tag (stored canonical)."
  locale: String
  "An IANA time zone name."
  zoneinfo: String
  "`YYYY-MM-DD`, a real date that is not in the future."
  birthdate: String
  address: AddressInput
}

extend type Query {
  """
  The users of a tenant (tenant viewer). `first` defaults to 25, at most 100.
  `email` finds the user with exactly that address (any case, spaces around
  ignored). `emailPrefix` keeps the users whose address, or username, starts
  with it (any case; plain text, never a pattern); blank means no filter. Give
  one of the two: both is BAD_USER_INPUT (400). `totalCount` follows the same
  filter.

  `roleId` keeps the users who hold the role; `attributes` keeps those whose
  value matches each filter (a choice or a boolean attribute, at most 5; a role
  attribute counts only while a held role links it). Every condition must hold,
  together with `emailPrefix` (at most 1 000 addresses may match the prefix, else
  BAD_USER_INPUT). Filtered pages follow the creation order; their cursor is the
  one the previous filtered page gave. A filter on an unknown, archived or
  unfit attribute, or an invalid option, is BAD_USER_INPUT (400).
  """
  users(
    tenantId: ID!
    after: String
    first: Int
    email: String
    emailPrefix: String
    roleId: ID
    attributes: [AttributeFilterInput!]
  ): TenantUserPage!
  """
  Finds users of a tenant for a picker (tenant admin, the permission that
  assigns roles). `query` matches the start of the e-mail address or username,
  or of the display name (any case, plain text, never a pattern); blank gives
  an empty list. `first` defaults to 10, at most 20. E-mail matches come first,
  then name matches; each user once. Only id, e-mail and name are returned. The
  name match uses janus's indexed name search, whatever the pool's size. A `query`
  over 254 characters is BAD_USER_INPUT (400).
  """
  userLookup(tenantId: ID!, query: String!, first: Int): [UserLookupResult!]!
  "One user of the tenant (tenant viewer), or `null`: unknown, or of another tenant."
  user(tenantId: ID!, id: ID!): TenantUser
  "The pending, unlapsed invitations into the tenant's user pool (tenant viewer)."
  userInvitations(tenantId: ID!): [UserInvitation!]!
  "The user's standing grants, oldest first (tenant viewer). Empty for an unknown user."
  userGrants(tenantId: ID!, userId: ID!): [UserGrant!]!
  "The user's standing sessions, newest first (tenant viewer). Empty for an unknown user."
  userSessions(tenantId: ID!, userId: ID!): [UserSession!]!
  """
  The data the console holds about a user, for their access request. Needs
  `edit` (it exposes personal data) and is recorded as `user.export`.
  Errors: NOT_FOUND (no such user).
  """
  userDataExport(tenantId: ID!, userId: ID!): UserDataExport!
}

extend type Mutation {
  """
  Invites an e-mail address into the tenant's user pool (tenant admin). The
  invitee accepts on the tenant's hosted `/invitation` page, which makes the
  account (e-mail proved), even when sign-up is closed. A pending invitation of
  the same address is replaced (a new mail goes out, after 60 s: INVITE_TOO_SOON 429 with `retryAfter` inside it;
  PENDING_INVITATIONS_LIMIT 409 past the pending cap for a new address). Errors: USER_EXISTS (409)
  when the address already has an account in the tenant, NOT_FOUND for an
  unknown tenant.
  """
  inviteUser(tenantId: ID!, email: EmailAddress!): UserInvitation!
  "Revokes a pending invitation of the tenant (tenant admin). True also when there is none."
  revokeInvitation(tenantId: ID!, invitationId: ID!): Boolean!
  """
  Updates a user's name and standard profile fields (tenant admin); the tenant's
  locks bind the user's own edits, not this one. Errors: BAD_USER_INPUT (400) for
  a name that is empty once trimmed or over 200 characters,
  PROFILE_FIELD_INVALID (400, with the field) for a malformed phone, locale,
  zoneinfo, birthdate, country or text, NOT_FOUND for an unknown user, CONFLICT
  (409) when the user changed meanwhile.
  The e-mail address and the verified flag are not editable.
  """
  updateUser(tenantId: ID!, userId: ID!, input: UpdateUserInput!): TenantUser!
  """
  Disables a user (tenant admin): their sessions end at once and they
  cannot sign in again. Idempotent. Errors: NOT_FOUND for
  an unknown user; on the `clavix` tenant, FORBIDDEN for an owner or a platform
  role holder unless the caller can manage the platform, LAST_OWNER (409) when
  the user is the only owner who can sign in of a tenant or of the platform
  (not on a repeat: a disabled user is not refused), CONFLICT (409) when
  the memberships keep changing (retry).
  """
  disableUser(tenantId: ID!, userId: ID!): TenantUser!
  "Enables a disabled user again (tenant admin). Idempotent. Errors: NOT_FOUND for an unknown user."
  enableUser(tenantId: ID!, userId: ID!): TenantUser!
  """
  Deletes a user for good (tenant admin): their sessions and grants (and the
  tokens those opened) go with them. True also when the user was already gone.
  On the `clavix` tenant the same FORBIDDEN, LAST_OWNER and CONFLICT errors as
  `disableUser` apply.
  """
  deleteUser(tenantId: ID!, userId: ID!): Boolean!
  "Ends every session of the user (tenant admin); answers how many it ended. 0 on a repeat or an unknown user."
  revokeUserSessions(tenantId: ID!, userId: ID!): Int!
  """
  Ends one session of the user (tenant admin). True when it was ended; false
  when it is not this user's, is already ended or lapsed, or does not exist.
  """
  revokeUserSession(tenantId: ID!, userId: ID!, sessionId: ID!): Boolean!
  """
  Marks the user's address verified or not (tenant admin), touching nothing
  else: no session, password or second factor changes. Idempotent. Errors:
  NOT_FOUND for an unknown user.
  """
  setUserEmailVerified(
    tenantId: ID!
    userId: ID!
    verified: Boolean!
  ): TenantUser!
  """
  Takes back one grant of the user and the tokens it opened (tenant admin).
  True also when the grant was already revoked; false when it is not this
  user's (or does not exist).
  """
  revokeGrant(tenantId: ID!, userId: ID!, grantId: ID!): Boolean!
  """
  Removes the user's TOTP second factor and recovery codes (tenant admin), for
  a user who lost the phone and the codes. Their sessions stay; the next
  sign-in no longer asks for a code. True or not, it is recorded; NOT_FOUND for
  an unknown user.
  """
  resetUserSecondFactor(tenantId: ID!, userId: ID!): TenantUser!
}
